\"2\"],false,[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],false,[9],false,[9],[9],[9],[19,\"3\"],false,[19,\"0\"],[19,\"1\"],[9],[9],[19,\"0\"],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],false,[9],[9],[9],[19,\"0\"],[9],[19,\"0\"],[9],[9],[9],[19,\"0\"],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9]]],[1,[5,\"updateReadReceipt\",[19,\"1794999885914\"],[19,\"156025504001094\"],[19,\"156025504001094\"],[19,\"0\"]]],[1,[5,\"insertXmaAttachment\",[9],[9],[19,\"0\"],false,[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[19,\"0\"],[9],[9],[9],[9],[19,\"156025504001094\"],[19,\"0\"],[19,\"7\"],\"\",[19,\"1794999885914\"],\"mid.$cAADXHFm2DOCoH5noWmh7lSfx8ft1\",[9],\"ee.mid.$cAADXHFm2DOCoH5noWmh7lSfx8ft1\",[19,\"0\"],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],\"# Exercise 3 \\u2014 CA by hand: how do students come to the university?\\n\\n*Table:*\\nResidence | Bus | Car | On foot | Total\\n**Town** | 20 | 30 | 50 | 100\\n**Village** | 60 | 30 | 10 | 100\\n**Total** | 80 | 60 | 60 | 200\\n### 1. Row profiles and average profile\\n\\nFormula: `Profile = row \\\/ row total`\\n | Bus | Car | On foot | Total\\n**Town** | $20\\\/100 = 0.20$ | $30\\\/100 = 0.30$ | $50\\\/100 = 0.50$ | 1\\n**Village** | $60\\\/100 = 0.60$ | $30\\\/100 = 0.30$ | $10\\\/100 = 0.10$ | 1\\n**Average profile** | $80\\\/200 = 0.40$ | $60\\\/200 = 0.30$ | $60\\\/200 = 0.30$ | 1\\n*What do you notice?*\\n- *Car* is identical everywhere: 30\\u0025 for Town, 30\\u0025 for Village, 30\\u0025 on average. It has no link with residence, it will be at the centre of the map.\\n- *Town:* walk a lot: 50\\u0025 vs 30\\u0025 on average.\\n- *Village:* take the bus a lot: 60\\u0025 vs 40\\u0025 on average.\\n- The two profiles are very different, so there is a strong association between residence and transport.\\n\\nRow masses: $r_{Town}=0.5$, $r_{Village}=0.5$. Column masses: $c = (0.4, 0.3, 0.3)$.\\n\\n### 2. Expected counts under independence and ratios Observed \\\/ Expected\\n\\nFormula: $E_{ij} = \\\\frac{\\\\text{Row total} \\\\times \\\\text{Column total}}{n}$\\nExpected | Bus | Car | On foot\\n**Town** | $100 \\\\times 80 \\\/ 200 = 40$ | $100 \\\\times 60 \\\/ 200 = 30$ | $100 \\\\times 60 \\\/ 200 = 30$\\n**Village** | $40$ | $30$ | $30$\\n*Ratio $O \\\/ E$:*\\nRatio $O\\\/E$ | Bus | Car | On foot\\n**Town** | $20\\\/40 = 0.50$ | $30\\\/30 = 1.00$ | $50\\\/30 = 1.67$\\n**Village** | $60\\\/40 = 1.50$ | $30\\\/30 = 1.00$ | $10\\\/30 = 0.33$\\n*Interpretation: Ratio > 1 = attraction, Ratio \\u003C 1 = repulsion*\\n\\n- *Town - On foot = 1.67 > 1:* strong attraction. Town students walk.\\n- *Village - Bus = 1.50 > 1:* strong attraction. Village students take the bus.\\n- *Town - Bus = 0.50* and *Village - On foot = 0.33:* strong repulsion, they are opposites.\\n- *Car = 1.00* everywhere: no attraction, no repulsion, independent.\\n\\n### 3. Chi-square, test of independence at 5\\u0025, total inertia, number of axes\\n\\nFormula: $\\\\chi^2 = \\\\sum \\\\frac{(O-E)^2}{E}$\\n\\nCell by cell:\\n- Town-Bus: $(20-40)^2 \\\/ 40 = 400\\\/40 = 10$\\n- Town-Car: $(30-30)^2 \\\/ 30 = 0$\\n- Town-On foot: $(50-30)^2 \\\/ 30 = 400\\\/30 = 13.33$\\n- Village-Bus: $(60-40)^2 \\\/ 40 = 10$\\n- Village-Car: $0$\\n- Village-On foot: $(10-30)^2 \\\/ 30 = 13.33$\\n\\\\chi^2 = 10 + 0 + 13.33 + 10 + 0 + 13.33 = 46.67\\n*Test of independence:*\\n- Degrees of freedom: $df = (2-1) \\\\times (3-1) = 2$\\n- Critical value at 5\\u0025: $\\\\chi^2_{critical} = 5.99$\\n- $46.67 > 5.99$ => *We reject independence.* There is a very strong association between residence and transport.\\n\\n*Total inertia:*\\n\\\\text{Total inertia} = \\\\frac{\\\\chi^2}{n} = \\\\frac{46.67}{200} = 0.2333\\n*Number of axes:*\\n\\\\text{Nb axes} = \\\\min(I-1, J-1) = \\\\min(1, 2) = 1\\nWe have *only one axis*, it explains 100\\u0025 of the inertia.\\n\\n### 4. Chi-square distance of Town and Village to the average profile\\n\\nFormula: $d^2(i, G) = \\\\sum_j \\\\frac{(profile_{ij} - \\\\bar{profile}_j)^2}{\\\\bar{profile}_j}$\\n\\n*For Town:*\\nd^2 = \\\\frac{(0.20-0.40)^2}{0.40} + \\\\frac{(0.30-0.30)^2}{0.30} + \\\\frac{(0.50-0.30)^2}{0.30}\\n= \\\\frac{0.04}{0.40} + 0 + \\\\frac{0.04}{0.30} = 0.10 + 0.1333 = 0.2333\\n*For Village:*\\nd^2 = \\\\frac{(0.60-0.40)^2}{0.40} + 0 + \\\\frac{(0.10-0.30)^2}{0.30} = 0.10 + 0.1333 = 0.2333\\n*Check of total inertia:*\\n\\\\text{Inertia} = \\\\sum_i r_i \\\\times d_i^2 = 0.5 \\\\times 0.2333 + 0.5 \\\\times 0.2333 = 0.2333\\nSame result as in Q3. Correct.\\n\\nTown and Village are at the same distance from the centre, on opposite sides.\\n\\n### 5. Gap matrix ( $S$), then $S S^T$. Find its eigenvalues and the eigenvalue of the CA\\n\\nWe build the matrix of standardized residuals $S$:\\nS_{ij} = \\\\frac{P_{ij} - r_i c_j}{\\\\sqrt{r_i c_j}} \\\\quad , \\\\quad P_{ij} = \\\\frac{N_{ij}}{200}\\nWe obtain:\\nS = \\\\begin{pmatrix} -0.224 & 0 & +0.258 \\\\\\\\ +0.224 & 0 & -0.258 \\\\end{pmatrix}\\nTo find the eigenvalues, we compute $S S^T$ (a $2 \\\\times 2$ matrix):\\nS S^T = \\\\begin{pmatrix} 0.1167 & -0.1167 \\\\\\\\ -0.1167 & 0.1167 \\\\end{pmatrix}\\n- *Trace =* $0.1167 + 0.1167 = 0.2333$\\n- *Determinant =* $0.1167 \\\\times 0.1167 - (-0.1167)^2 = 0$\\n\\nThe eigenvalues $\\\\lambda$ are solutions of: $\\\\lambda^2 - \\\\text{Trace}\\\\times \\\\lambda + \\\\text{Det} = 0$\\n\\\\lambda^2 - 0.2333 \\\\lambda = 0\\n\\\\lambda_1 = 0.2333 \\\\quad , \\\\quad \\\\lambda_2 = 0\\n*The eigenvalue of the CA is $\\\\lambda_1 = 0.2333$*, which is exactly the total inertia, and it explains 100\\u0025.\\n\\n### 6. Coordinates of rows and columns, map (one axis) and recommendation\\n\\n*Row coordinates:*\\nF_{Town} = -0.483 \\\\quad , \\\\quad F_{Village} = +0.483\\n*Column coordinates* (by the barycentric \\\/ transition relation: $G_j = \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda_1}} \\\\sum_i \\\\text{col-profile}_{ij} \\\\times F_i$):\\n | Bus | Car | On foot\\n**Coordinate** | **+0.50** | **0** | **-0.67**\\n*Map - one axis:*\\nOn foot (-0.67)   Town (-0.48)   Car (0)   Village (+0.48)   Bus (+0.50)\\n----------------|----------------|-----------|----------------|----------------->\\n      \\u25c4--- Town students ---\\u25ba      \\u25c4--- Village students ---\\u25ba\\n*Reading:*\\n- On the left: *Town and On foot* together.\\n- On the right: *Village and Bus* together.\\n- Exactly in the centre: *Car*, with no association.\\n\\n*Recommendation for the university:*\\n\\n> *The university should add bus lines for the Village, not for the Town.*\\n> Village students depend heavily on the bus (60\\u0025 of them), while Town students mainly walk (50\\u0025 of them) and do not need the bus as much. Car use is not linked to residence.\\n\\nThis is the complete CA in one axis.\",\"\",[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[19,\"0\"],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],[9],\"{\\\"layout_type\\\":\\\"SINGLE\\\",\\\"content_type\\\":3040,\\\"is_shareable\\\":false,\\\"content\\\":{\\\"custom_template_data\\\":{\\\"sections\\\":[],\\\"unified_response\\\":{\\\"response_id\\\":\\\"0cec2544-9eda-4594-aa36-b14d78d58c63\\\",\\\"sections\\\":[{\\\"view_model\\\":{\\\"primitive\\\":{\\\"text\\\":\\\"# Exercise 3 \\\\u2014 CA by hand: how do students come to the university?\\\\n\\\\n*Table:*\\\",\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"GenAIMarkdownTextUXPrimitive\\\"},\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"GenAISingleLayoutViewModel\\\"}},{\\\"view_model\\\":{\\\"primitive\\\":{\\\"rows\\\":[{\\\"is_header\\\":true,\\\"cells\\\":[\\\"Residence\\\",\\\"Bus\\\",\\\"Car\\\",\\\"On foot\\\",\\\"Total\\\"],\\\"markdown_cells\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Residence\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Bus\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Car\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"On foot\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Total\\\"}]},{\\\"is_header\\\":false,\\\"cells\\\":[\\\"**Town**\\\",\\\"20\\\",\\\"30\\\",\\\"50\\\",\\\"100\\\"],\\\"markdown_cells\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"*Town*\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"20\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"30\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"50\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"100\\\"}]},{\\\"is_header\\\":false,\\\"cells\\\":[\\\"**Village**\\\",\\\"60\\\",\\\"30\\\",\\\"10\\\",\\\"100\\\"],\\\"markdown_cells\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"*Village*\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"60\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"30\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"10\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"100\\\"}]},{\\\"is_header\\\":false,\\\"cells\\\":[\\\"**Total**\\\",\\\"80\\\",\\\"60\\\",\\\"60\\\",\\\"200\\\"],\\\"markdown_cells\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"*Total*\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"80\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"60\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"60\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"200\\\"}]}],\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"GenATableUXPrimitive\\\"},\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"GenAISingleLayoutViewModel\\\"}},{\\\"view_model\\\":{\\\"primitive\\\":{\\\"text\\\":\\\"### 1. Row profiles and average profile\\\\n\\\\nFormula: `Profile = row \\\\\\\/ row total`\\\",\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"GenAIMarkdownTextUXPrimitive\\\"},\\\"__typename\\\":\\\"GenAISingleLayoutViewModel\\\"}},{\\\"view_model\\\":{\\\"primitive\\\":{\\\"rows\\\":[{\\\"is_header\\\":true,\\\"cells\\\":[\\\"\\\",\\\"Bus\\\",\\\"Car\\\",\\\"On foot\\\",\\\"Total\\\"],\\\"markdown_cells\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Bus\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Car\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"On foot\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Total\\\"}]},{\\\"is_header\\\":false,\\\"cells\\\":[\\\"**Town**\\\",\\\"$20\\\\\\\/100 = 0.20$\\\",\\\"$30\\\\\\\/100 = 0.30$\\\",\\\"$50\\\\\\\/100 = 0.50$\\\",\\\"1\\\"],\\\"markdown_cells\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"*Town*\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"{{IE_0}}$20\\\\\\\/100 = 0.20${{\\\\\\\/IE_0}}\\\",\\\"inline_entities\\\":[{\\\"key\\\":\\\"IE_0\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"latex_image\\\":{\\\"url\\\":\\\"https:\\\\\\\/\\\\\\\/scontent.xx.fbcdn.net\\\\\\\/v\\\\\\\/t58.90637-6\\\\\\\/912402754_3012972715749791_4607161557200908216_n.png\\\\\\\/